# golden: bash _fzf_rows output, frozen 2026-09-02 before the fzf code
# was deleted. Regenerating this is not possible any more, and that is
# the point: it is the layout specification now. See tests/run.sh.
#
# ONE case has been superseded since, deliberately and on the record: a
# summary too long for the window used to run past the right edge and
# take the path, agent and version columns off the screen with it. It is
# cut with an ellipsis now instead. The frozen file had it both ways: its
# own header calls those columns "pinned to the right edge, in fixed
# columns, so it costs the summary no width", which is the behaviour here
# and was never what the code did. It went unnoticed while every summary
# came from a pane title, a handful of words; a PAST session's summary is
# whatever it was asked to do, up to eighty characters, and those rows
# arrived pushing the table out of the window. 108 lines, rows %13 and
# %17, at widths 99, 100 and 130. Nothing else in this file has moved.
